What is the historical context and significance of Kolel Chibas Jerusalem in the Jewish community?
Kolel Chibas Yerushalayim, also known as the Charity of Rabbi Meyer Ba'al Ha-Nes, is a charitable organization established in 1830 in Jerusalem's Meah Shearim neighborhood. It was founded by Jews from Galicia, a region spanning southeastern Poland and western Ukraine, to support full-time Torah students of the Yishuv haYashan. The organization received widespread support from the Galician Jewish community and later expanded its collection network to other parts of Europe and America. The Kolel has played a significant role in supporting Jews who have emigrated to the Holy Land, particularly from Galicia, and has been led by notable rabbis and community leaders throughout its history.
